    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S6824\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act in relation to granting Nancy Porretto Tier IV\nstatus in the New York state and local employees' retirement system\nwith a membership date of September 1, 2005\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nAt the request of the Bedford Central School District, this bill\nallows Nancy Porretto to apply for Tier IV status in the New York\nState and Local Employees' Retirement System.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Allows Nancy Porretto to apply for retroactive membership\nin the New York State and Local Employees' Retirement System with an\neffective date of September 1, 2005, at which point she will be deemed\nto have Tier IV status in such system.\n\nSection 2: States that all past employer costs of implementing the\nprovisions of this act shall be borne by the Bedford Central School\nDistrict.\n\nSection 3: Provides an effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNancy Porretto was employed as a full-time staff member by the Bedford\nCentral School District on September 1, 2005. However, despite her\nsubmittal of an application to Bedford school officials.  Ms. Porretto\nfailed to become a member of the New York State and Local Employees'\nRetirement System. The Bedford Central School District takes full\nresponsibility for this oversight, and at their request, this\nlegislation allows Ms. Porretto to receive the tier status she should\nhave received on September 1, 2005. It should be noted that all past\nemployer costs of implementing the provisions of this act shall be\nborne by the Bedford Central School District.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nFiscal note attached.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
